course: dictionary
lesson: 10503
title: Twentieth: order, fraction or century
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Twentieth comes right after nineteenth in order, so it is number 20. If you are twentieth in a line, nineteen people are in front of you.
explain: Twentieth can also be a part of a whole. One twentieth means one of twenty equal parts, written 1/20. «Recycling an aluminium can uses only about a twentieth of the energy needed to make a new one from rock.» The clue is only about a twentieth: a very small part of the energy. To check, divide by 20: 1 ÷ 20 = 0.05, which is 5%.
explain: In history, the twentieth century means a hundred years of history, the time of the first cars, planes and computers. Look for the words around it, such as century or years, to tell which meaning is used. «Let the jury consider their verdict,» says the King, for about the twentieth time. Here the clue is time: the King is counting how many times he has said it.
fact: Twentieth is the order word for 20th, so it comes after nineteenth.
fact: One twentieth is written 1/20, and it means one of twenty equal parts.
fact: To find a twentieth of a number, divide it by 20.
fact: One twentieth is the same as 0.05, which is 5%.
fact: The twentieth century is a hundred years of history, the time of the first cars, planes and computers.
exercise: Anna finishes in the twentieth place in a race. How many runners finish ahead of her? | 20 | 1 | 21 | *19
exercise: One twentieth of a cake is what fraction? | 1/10 | 1/2 | *1/20 | 20/1
exercise: «Recycling an aluminium can uses only about a twentieth of the energy needed to make a new one from rock.» What does a twentieth mean here? | Twenty whole cans | The twentieth can in a row | Twice as much energy | *A small part, one of twenty equal parts
test: What is the twentieth century? | A year that ends in 20 | A hundred cars in a row | A type of computer | *A hundred years of history, with the first cars, planes and computers
test: «Let the jury consider their verdict,» says the King, for about the twentieth time. What does the twentieth time mean? | Twenty times at once | *The twentieth time it has happened, in order | A twentieth of a second | The first time ever
exam: One twentieth is the same as which percentage? | 20% | *5% | 50% | 1%
